"helpHeading" = "SpreadsheetHelper Help";
"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Select cells in Microsoft Excel, or in Google Sheets opened in a browser (Google Chrome, Safari, Firefox).\n2. Press **⌥⌘C**. SpreadsheetHelper sends Copy (⌘C) to the app, cleans the copied text and puts it back on the clipboard.\n3. Paste with ⌘V.\n- The result is shown briefly at the top of the screen and kept as “Last result” in the main window and at the top of the menu bar menu. On failure the clipboard is not changed.\n- ⌥⌘C is registered only while a target app is in front, so other apps keep their own ⌥⌘C. The front app is checked again right after the key press.\n\n## What is cleaned\n### Microsoft Excel\n- Formatting is removed (plain text).\n- A leading “‑” (U+2011 non-breaking hyphen) + run of “_” + one whitespace is removed at each line start (regex (?m)^‑_+\\s, case-insensitive).\n- Cells that Excel wraps in quotes (for example, cells with line breaks) lose the outer quotes, and \"\" inside becomes \" (judged per tab-separated cell).\n### Google Sheets (Chrome, Safari, Firefox)\nRemoves the quotes added when copying cells that contain line breaks, in this order, then writes plain text:\n1. Remove \" at the start of each line\n2. Remove \" at the end of each line\n3. Collapse runs of \" into one\n4. Replace ' (apostrophe) with \" (can be turned off in Settings > Target Apps)\n- Example: \"a(newline)b\" → a(newline)b, a\"\"b → a\"b\n- ※ Only line starts and ends are handled, so quotes of a cell in the middle of a tab-separated row may remain.\n- ※ Cleaning runs only while a Google Sheets window (title contains “Google Sheets”, etc.) is in front. On other pages ⌥⌘C is passed on to the browser (for example, Chrome's Inspect Elements).\n\n## Restore\n- “Restore Original Copy” (main window, File menu, menu bar) puts back the content before cleaning (text, HTML, RTF). Images and other formats are not restored.\n- Nothing is restored after another copy. The content is kept in memory only and discarded on quit.\n\n## Settings\n- Startup & Background: launch at login (off by default), Hide from Dock and App Switcher (off by default; when on, the app appears in the Dock and ⌘Tab while main/settings windows exist, including minimized windows, and hides after all such windows close; show it from the menu bar icon or by opening it again in Finder), keep running after closing, show in menu bar, Accessibility status, restart and quit buttons.\n- Hotkey: enable or disable ⌥⌘C, pause until relaunch, Change… records a key with ⌘ or ⌃ (Esc cancels), Reset to Default, success notification.\n- Target Apps: turn each of the four apps on or off (all on by default), apostrophe replacement.\n- About: version and links.\n- Open Settings with ⌘, and close it with ⌘W.\n\n## Hotkeys\n- **⌥⌘C**: copy and clean (only while a target app is in front).\n- Duplicates within this app and registration failures are shown in Settings. Not every conflict with other apps can be detected.\n\n## Table commands\nTurn each on or off and change its key in Settings ▸ Hotkey. The keys below are the defaults. A key you record must include ⌘ or ⌃ (rows whose default is ⌥V, ⌥←, ⌥→ or ⌥⇧= also accept ⌥ alone), and cannot be one the app already uses.\n### Excel and Google Sheets\n- **⌃I**: Insert rows or columns\n- **⌃K**: Delete rows or columns\n- **⌘3**: Hide rows or columns\n- **⌥⌘P**: Insert pivot table\n### Excel only\n- **⇧⌘E**: Center cells\n- **⇧⌘L**: Align left\n- **⇧⌘R**: Align right\n- **⌘G**: Center across selection\n- **⇧⌘G**: Undo center across selection\n- **⌃⌥Home**: Jump to A1\n- **⌃U**: Edit cell from the start\n- **⌘F**: Replace...\n- **⌥V**: Paste Special...\n- **⌥⌘K**: Clear hyperlinks\n- **⌥⌘W**: Add borders to selection\n- **⌃⌥⌘I**: Power Query (Get Data)\n- **⌃⌘N**: New window\n### Google Sheets only\n- **⌥←**: Previous sheet\n- **⌥→**: Next sheet\n- **⌥⇧=**: SUM function\n- **⌃⇧1**: Number format (#,##0)\n- **⌃⌥⌘=**: Header row (freeze, bold and center row 1)\n- **⌃F**: Alternating colors\n- **⌃⇧6**: Middle align and wrap\n- **⌃⌥⌘F**: Format special (middle, wrap, header row, alternating colors)\n- **⌃⇧F**: Create a filter\n### Notes\n- ⌃I and ⌃K pick rows or columns from the selection. In Excel, ⌘3 hides rows when whole rows are selected, otherwise columns.\n- Alignment (left, right, center across selection), the ⌘3 check and Jump to A1 control Excel with AppleScript. You are asked for permission the first time.\n- In browsers, only a Google Sheets window is handled; on other pages the key is passed through. When Excel cannot run the menu item (for example while editing a cell), the key goes to Excel unchanged.\n\n## Accessibility permission\nNeeded to send ⌘C to the target app. Turn on SpreadsheetHelper in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility. Settings > Startup & Background has a button that opens it. Without permission, ⌥⌘C shows the reason and does nothing.\n\n## Staying in the menu bar and quitting\n- The table icon in the menu bar offers the main window, Settings, Pause, Restore, Help and Quit. Hide the icon with Menu Bar Settings… in the app menu (the app keeps running).\n- Closing the window keeps the app running. Reopening it from the Dock or Finder shows the main window.\n- Quit with “Quit SpreadsheetHelper” (app menu, menu bar, Settings > Startup & Background) or ⌘Q while the app is in front.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- “Copy failed”: make sure cells are selected and you are not editing a cell. The run stops if the clipboard does not change within 1 second.\n- Nothing happens: check in Settings that the target app is on, the hotkey is enabled and not paused.\n- Still shown as not allowed after granting: restart the app. If that does not help, remove SpreadsheetHelper from the list in System Settings and add it again.\n\n## Sharing settings\n- In Settings › Sharing, Export & Import saves the settings to a file (SpreadsheetHelper-Settings.plist) or reads them back, for moving to another Mac or keeping a backup. Importing asks before replacing.\n- Settings Sync keeps the settings in a folder such as iCloud Drive or Dropbox; Macs that choose the same folder share the settings, and the most recent save wins.\n- Shared: the hotkeys, the table commands, the target apps and the cleaning options. Launch at login, staying open and the menu bar icon stay on each Mac.\n\n## Privacy\nNo network communication (update checks stay off until an update feed is configured). Clipboard content is never logged or sent.\n\n## Uninstall\nDelete SpreadsheetHelper from Applications. To remove settings, also delete ~/Library/Preferences/jp.dtp-transit.spreadsheethelper.plist, and remove the app from Login Items and the Accessibility list.\nManual launch and reopening show the main window; automatic login launch does not.\n\n\n## Dock visibility and application menus\n\nMain and settings windows keep the app in the Dock and ⌘Tab so its application menus remain available. Minimized windows stay listed. Close all such windows to hide it; palettes alone do not show it. Your saved setting is preserved.";
